## Repair pass (d3fda61 shipped red - fixing)

The d3fda61 commit did NOT compile (10 errors) and its "5 named TDD tests"
were nested INSIDE the aggregate `ra_specials_each_deterministic` fn body as
plain nested fns - never collected, never run. Fixes:

1. Module imports for dog/medic/engineer/tanya/madtank added to game.rs.
2. `update_unit_combat` rewritten to index-based iteration (the codebase's
   facings pattern) so the dog branch can call `self.apply_damage`.
3. Dog bite resolves the ordered victim directly from `self.units` (the
   enemies snapshot is house-shroud dependent and missed at shroud-off).
4. Tanya C4 demolition arm added against structures (tanya::tanya_demolition_damage).
5. Specials now run BEFORE the weapon gate: Tanya/medic carry no weapon row,
   so `let Some(weapon) = weapon else continue` skipped them entirely.
6. The 5 nested fake tests were extricated into real top-level #[test] fns.
7. `deflect_chance_percent = 0` set in dog/tanya tests: apply_damage draws a
   deflect roll per damage event, so the bite/demolition was nondeterministic.
8. `madtank_detonates_after_charge` asserts the module constants +
   mad_tank_sequence; the sim detonation exists in update_special_units but
   `madtank::is_mad_tank` returns false unconditionally (no MAD ClassId in the
   roster) so the in-sim path is currently unreachable - documented, not faked.

NOT IMPLEMENTED (documented gap): Tanya twin pistols vs infantry have no
weapon row for InfantryE11 in GameUnit::new, so the sim cannot express them;
the C4-vs-structure behavior is the implemented half.

